Stage B — Fixed-Point Integer Engine (main_stageB_fixedpoint.c)
Definition:
Replace 64-bit floating-point double prices and quantities 
with 64-bit scaled integers (long long multiplied by 10^8) 
and evaluate SMA crossovers using pure integer 
cross-multiplication.

Analysis:
1. Executes SMA running-sum updates and crossover checks 
((sum_short * LONG_N) - (sum_long * SHORT_N)) 
on standard Integer ALUs without floating-point division.

2. Runs in 126.85 ms (7.88M trades/sec)—more than 2.19x faster
than the naive double engine—while still updating double VWAP
and OHLC bars for equal workload comparison.

3. Scaling by 10^8 preserves 8 decimal places of precision
and achieves 100% identical crossover signals 
(2292 BUY / 2286 SELL) with zero floating-point drift.

Algorithm Design:
BEGIN
    open DEV dataset
    trade_count <- 0

    WHILE trade_count < 1000000 AND read_trade(raw_ts, raw_price, raw_qty, raw_buy)
        trades_fp[trade_count].ts <- raw_ts
        trades_fp[trade_count].price_fp <- raw_price * 100000000 + 0.5
        trades_fp[trade_count].qty_fp <- raw_qty * 100000000 + 0.5
        trades_fp[trade_count].is_buy <- raw_buy
        trade_count <- trade_count + 1
    ENDWHILE
    close trades

    short_sma <- 0
    long_sma <- 0
    vwap <- 0
    ohlc <- 0
    sig_st <- 0
    buy_signals <- 0
    sell_signals <- 0
    open "plots/signals_stageB_fp.dat"

    start_time <- now_ns()

    FOR i <- 0 TO trade_count - 1
        READ ts, p_fp, q_fp from trades_fp[i]
        update vwap, ohlc using (p_fp / 100000000)
        update short_sma, long_sma with p_fp
        signal <- SIGNAL_NONE
        IF short_sma is full AND long_sma is full THEN
            d <- (short_sma.running_sum * LONG_N) - (long_sma.running_sum * SHORT_N)
            signal <- crossover check using d
        ENDIF
        IF signal = SIGNAL_BUY THEN
            buy_signals <- buy_signals + 1
        ENDIF
        IF signal = SIGNAL_SELL THEN
            sell_signals <- sell_signals + 1
        ENDIF
        IF (i + 1) >= 10000 AND (i + 1) <= 12000 THEN
            PRINT (i + 1), price, s_val, l_val, signal to file
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR

    end_time <- now_ns()
    close file
    elapsed_ns <- end_time - start_time
    elapsed_ms <- elapsed_ns / 1000000
    ns_per_trade <- elapsed_ns / trade_count
    trades_per_sec <- trade_count / (elapsed_ns / 1000000000)
    PRINT trade_count, buy_signals, sell_signals, elapsed_ns, elapsed_ms, ns_per_trade, trades_per_sec
END